WEBVTT

00:01:28.038 --> 00:01:31.246
And it's not just behavioral symptoms.

00:01:31.288 --> 00:01:35.288
Depression has physical manifestations
inside the brain.

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:36.454
First of all,

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.121
there are changes that could be seen
with the naked eye

00:01:39.163 --> 00:01:40.454
and X-ray vision.

00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:44.871
These include smaller frontal lobes
and hippocampal volumes.

00:01:45.454 --> 00:01:46.871
On a more microscale,

00:01:46.913 --> 00:01:49.288
depression is associated
with a few things:

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:53.246
the abnormal transmission or depletion
of certain neurotransmitters,

00:01:53.288 --> 00:01:57.871
especially serotonin, 
norepinephrine, and dopamine,

00:01:57.913 --> 00:01:59.538
blunted circadian rhythms,

00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:02.913
or specific changes in the REM
and slow-wave parts of your sleep cycle,